      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin the process for the P&E Court, start by Listing and then proceed."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the process initiation and the initial listing/proceeding step. Structural init and restated actions preserve the original behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3",
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After that, receive the Court Calendar and Check the Availability of the P&E Judge."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly splits and maps the two compound steps described in this unit."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "When checking the P&E Judge Availability, make sure to consider all judges."
      ],
      "justification": "Faithful paraphrase of the requirement to include all judges in the availability check."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6",
        "action:n7",
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the availability is checked, Resolve any issues with the P&E Judge Availability and then continue with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the implicit check, resolution, and continuation. Treating the condition as an explicit question/action and splitting the flow preserves the intended behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9",
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, make any necessary changes to the P&E Schedules before concluding the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Covers the final schedule adjustments and process conclusion. Redundant termination action and structural end node do not alter behaviour."
    }
